# `yo fix <path> --migrate explicit-copy` at a closure capture list
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-21-explicit-copy-rewrites-a-capture-list-shorthand-into-an-unparseable-clone.md).
# The shorthand entry `{ s }` names the capture and its source together, so
# its copy is spelled `{ s : s.clone() }`; the run used to append to the name,
# `{ s.clone() }`, which does not parse (E0007). The entry `{ seen }` is
# written in the closure body (`seen.push`) and the caller reads that write
# (`seen.len()` is 1): the copy is written afterwards, so the site is listed,
# not cloned (a clone would print `4 4 0`). The expected_tree pins the
# rewritten main.yo, and the trailing `check` proves it still evaluates.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=240
